 {
  "id": "evt_d17b49fdcf194467a31544d9f2a9bf45",
  "kind": "plan",
  "source": "agent",
  "timestamp": "2026-06-11T04:59:17.738699Z",
  "schema_version": 1,
  "seq": 8,
  "meta": {},
  "summary": "Build a sensor dashboard: Python API (port 3000) serving CSV as JSON, and a Vite+React frontend (port 8000) with a data table and summary card.",
  "steps": [
   {
    "title": "Create Python backend API",
    "detail": "Write a single-file Flask app (server.py) that reads uploads/sensor_readings.csv and serves it as JSON at GET /api/readings on port 3000. Install flask via pip."
   },
   {
    "title": "Scaffold Vite + React frontend",
    "detail": "Create the React app in a /frontend directory using Vite (npm create vite), install dependencies, and configure proxy in vite.config.js so /api requests forward to port 3000."
   },
   {
    "title": "Build dashboard UI components",
    "detail": "Create App.jsx that fetches /api/readings on mount, renders a summary card (count, min temp, max temp) and a scrollable table with columns: timestamp, sensor, temperature."
   },
   {
    "title": "Start both servers and verify in browser",
    "detail": "Start the Flask API on port 3000, then start the Vite dev server on port 8000. Verify the page loads, the table populates, and the summary card shows correct stats."
   }
  ],
  "revision": 1,
  "context": "## What I found\n\n- **CSV data**: `uploads/sensor_readings.csv` has 200 rows, 3 columns: `timestamp`, `sensor`, `temperature_c`. Sensors include nvme, amdgpu, k10temp, spd5118.\n- **Workspace**: Empty aside from the uploaded CSV \u2014 fresh start.\n\n## Approach\n\n- **Backend**: Flask (lightweight Python web framework) \u2014 one file, reads CSV with Python's `csv` module, returns JSON array. Runs on port 3000.\n- **Frontend**: Vite + React \u2014 fast dev server, minimal config. Uses Vite's built-in proxy (`server.proxy`) to forward `/api/*` to `http://localhost:3000`, so the React app calls `/api/readings` and Vite routes it to Flask.\n- **Summary card**: Computes count, min temperature, max temperature from the fetched data.\n- **Table**: Simple styled HTML table showing all readings.\n\n## Trade-offs\n\n- Flask over Node because the CSV parsing is trivially simple in Python and avoids an extra runtime dependency.\n- Vite proxy avoids CORS issues and keeps the frontend code clean (no `http://localhost:3000` hardcoded)."
 },
